{
  "adjustments": [
    {
      "target": "u1",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "The whole update is supported by current runs. `P8:12` applies `heat apple 1 with microwave 1` while holding apple 1 and succeeds at `P8:14`; by contrast `P9:14`/`P9:16` and `P10:45`/`P10:47` move the object into the microwave, close it and repeatedly toggle the door without invoking heat, ending at `step_limit` (group `G4`). The cool clause is likewise followed to success in `P3:8`/`P3:10`, `P4:45`/`P4:47`, `P6:40`/`P6:43` and `P7:18`/`P7:20`, and `P6:40` shows cooling works while the fridge is still closed, so no door-toggling prerequisite is implied. No supplied evidence contradicts the negative clause; `M2` only reports preserved post-acquisition transform-place sequences in a different batch and does not call for changing this update. Retaining triggers, actions and boundary.",
      "to": null
    },
    {
      "target": "u2",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "`P5` (task 'cool some pan') takes `pot 1` at `P5:28`, an object of the wrong type, and repeatedly moves it to `stoveburner 1` at `P5:29`, `P5:36` and `P5:43` without changing object or target, ending at `step_limit`; this is exactly the wrong-type-plus-repetition failure the update targets (group `G2`). `P7` shows the recovery direction working: after moving `pan 1` to `countertop 1` does not end the task at `P7:11`, it switches to `pot 2` at `P7:16`, cools it at `P7:18` and succeeds at `P7:20`. When the required type is not visible, the needed coverage is already supplied by `u3`, so `u2` needs no scope change and no duplicated search clause. Both clauses are retained.",
      "to": null
    },
    {
      "target": "u3",
      "focus": ["S", "C"],
      "change": "Retain the pre-acquisition search direction, but make it systematic and executable: search closed containers by opening cabinets, drawers and the fridge/microwave and checking shelves, choosing a container or surface not already checked rather than one your recent observations already showed empty; explicitly cover the container types you have not yet opened before concluding the object is unavailable; and bound the anti-revisit guidance to the period before the required object is acquired so that the post-acquisition return to a fridge/sink for the required transform is not blocked.",
      "reason": "Direction is retained and directly supported: `P2` never finds bread and ends at `step_limit`, opening the fridge/microwave and cabinets 1-3 and 5 while repeatedly rechecking fridge 1 (`P2:5`, `P2:16`, `P2:27`, `P2:48`), yet never opening any drawer or checking any shelf although `C9` offers `go to drawer 1..9` and `go to shelf 1..3` (group `G1`). Historical knowledge shows the same direction was only partially effective and points to a scope limit: `M2` reports a candidate that cycled among inspected locations and never visited an in-scene plausible surface (`S1_R02/Q8:50`), while `M1` reports both continued rechecking of known-empty shelves (`S1_R01/Q7:6` through `S1_R01/Q7:15`) and a case with fewer redundant rechecks (`S1_R01/Q8:13`). Because the Actor only sees the last two observations and actions, 'unvisited' must be read relative to recent observations, so the new text makes container-type coverage and the recent-empty preference explicit. The pre-acquisition bound coordinates with `u1`/`u2`, which require returning the acquired object to the appliance and then the named target. The historical mechanism comes from a different batch and object domain, so its transfer is an unverified hypothesis; the current `P2` gap is the direct ground for strengthening coverage. Choice of strength (systematic coverage, not exhaustive enumeration) is a judgment to test under the 50-step budget.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n-- When the required object is not visible on surfaces reached so far, search closed containers by opening drawers and cabinets (and the fridge/microwave) and check shelves, moving to unvisited containers rather than re-checking locations already shown to be empty.\n+- When the required object is not visible on surfaces reached so far, search closed containers systematically: open cabinets, drawers, and the fridge/microwave and check shelves, choosing a container or surface you have not yet checked rather than returning to one your recent observations already showed empty.\n - Countertops and diningtables reveal their contents directly when reached, so visit unvisited surfaces before returning to already-seen ones.\n+- Cover the container types you have not yet opened before concluding the object is unavailable, and move to a different unvisited container or surface instead of reopening one just shown empty.\n+- Apply this search guidance only until the required object is acquired; once you have it, proceed with the required transform and placement steps rather than continuing to search.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "u4",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "Many current actions are malformed: empty (`P2:1`, `P4:4`, `P5:48`), `...` (`P2:6`, `P5:41`, `P9:21`) or reasoning text embedded in the action field (`P2:2`, `P3:5`, `P4:28`, `P6:33`, `P7:3`). Memory `M1` reports that adding admissible-action clauses was associated with fewer malformed actions in several paired runs (`S1_R01/P1:14` vs `S1_R01/Q1:11`; `S1_R01/P4:5` vs `S1_R01/Q4:5`; `S1_R01/P8:5` vs `S1_R01/Q8:15`) even though compliance was not uniform (`S1_R01/Q3:11`, `S1_R01/Q3:20`). That non-uniform compliance is not a reason to weaken or to repeat the requirement more forcefully, so the clause is retained as written.",
      "to": null
    }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "update_ids": ["u1"],
      "question": "When a hot/cool object is required, does the Actor hold the object and invoke `heat`/`cool` with the appliance directly, rather than moving it into the appliance and toggling its door?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "update_ids": ["u2"],
      "question": "Does the Actor select an object matching the task's named type, and after a placement that does not end the task, does it change the object or target instead of repeating the same combination?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "update_ids": ["u3"],
      "question": "When the required object is not on visible surfaces, does the Actor open and check closed containers across the container types it has not yet opened (cabinets, drawers, shelves, fridge/microwave) rather than re-checking locations recently shown empty, and does it stop searching and proceed to the transform and placement once the object is acquired?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "update_ids": ["u4"],
      "question": "Does each step contain exactly one verbatim admissible command, with no empty, placeholder, or reasoning-text actions and no illegal targets?"
    }
  ]
}
